{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531131-some-thoughts-about-artifacts-in-v20-v2","id":1531131,"title":"Some thoughts about artifacts in V20/V2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-19T11:45:26-08:00","id":1531131,"title":"Some thoughts about artifacts in V20/V2","content":"For instance i saw that hand of conrad increases potence,brawl and courage.Just not sure how to rule it whether its +1 to potence or grants +2 to all potence,brawl and courage checks.For instance giants blood is said to give temporary potence and sometimes maybe even permanenth potence.How would anyone of you here rule those two artifacts and if anyone has any homebrew artifacts would be cool to post them here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4185-ragnor","name":"Ragnor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T13:12:30-08:00","id":1531137,"title":"","content":"The Kindred of the East offshoot splat for Vampire had an entire crafting system for making artifacts so that would be a good place to start. Though it was mostly a reskinned system from Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Vampires are one of those critters that would gain the most from magical infrastructure and equipment, but it is rarely applied to them despite the long lifespan allowing for collecting the items or just learning how to produce them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T12:52:48-08:00","id":1531246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531131-some-thoughts-about-artifacts-in-v20-v2?p=1531137#post1531137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kindred of the East offshoot splat for Vampire had an entire crafting system for making artifacts so that would be a good place to start. Though it was mostly a reskinned system from Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Vampires are one of those critters that would gain the most from magical infrastructure and equipment, but it is rarely applied to them despite the long lifespan allowing for collecting the items or just learning how to produce them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks alot m8 checked the artifacts they are interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4185-ragnor","name":"Ragnor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T01:40:21-07:00","id":1536955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531131-some-thoughts-about-artifacts-in-v20-v2#post1531131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance i saw that hand of conrad increases potence,brawl and courage.Just not sure how to rule it whether its +1 to potence or grants +2 to all potence,brawl and courage checks.For instance giants blood is said to give temporary potence and sometimes maybe even permanenth potence.How would anyone of you here rule those two artifacts and if anyone has any homebrew artifacts would be cool to post them here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Artifacts should be potent, but not &quot;I WIN&quot; buttons. And they should be incredibly difficult to obtain, and more importantly, extremely difficult to MAINTAIN. As in a very potent curse, as in every kill takes more of the user's soul, or kills one the user's friends/family, or their puppies/kittens, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Such items can destroy a session. Roleplaying games are really about socialization: hanging out. This ain't a min/max uber build vidya gaym. Items that are insta-kill/win should not be allowed, and if they are, they should be one use, very costly items, and a time and discretion of the Game Master/Dungeon Master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T20:53:15-07:00","id":1540194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531131-some-thoughts-about-artifacts-in-v20-v2?p=1536955#post1536955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Artifacts should be potent, but not &quot;I WIN&quot; buttons. And they should be incredibly difficult to obtain, and more importantly, extremely difficult to MAINTAIN. As in a very potent curse, as in every kill takes more of the user's soul, or kills one the user's friends/family, or their puppies/kittens, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Such items can destroy a session. Roleplaying games are really about socialization: hanging out. This ain't a min/max uber build vidya gaym. Items that are insta-kill/win should not be allowed, and if they are, they should be one use, very costly items, and a time and discretion of the Game Master/Dungeon Master.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I guess we now know Justin Achilli's username on this forum, lol jk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-12-2024, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T15:28:54-07:00","id":1540229,"title":"","content":"A direct bonus to a Discipline is likely a bad idea. Having an effect directly modeled from a Discipline, isn't. You could have an item that gives you the same effect of Potence 2, but someone already with Potence would receive less or no benefit at all.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I usually borrow the systems of other splats when I want something, or even if the player decides to search for something.<br /> <br /> In fact, if a player wants a magical item at the start, I'm amenable to discussing the simple purchase of an item related Background from another line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T18:23:13-07:00","id":1540253,"title":"","content":"I personally never bothered with artifacts myself as I could never find a good reason of why it would be helpful to my character. Then again I'm not a big fan of Blood Sorcery or the related stuff with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T21:59:32-07:00","id":1540262,"title":"","content":"A few easy ways to keep an Artifact from unbalancing a game is to make it not easily portable, easy to damage, or just have specific requirements to activate.<br /> <br /> In one Tremere game, we had an Auspex specialist who really wanted to lean into the Seer/Prophet concept. As a result, we had a game to build a custom artifact that was a meditation throne which reduced the difficulty on Auspex related rolls when one was seated on it and helped protect the user when Astral Projecting.<br /> <br /> It was big and ornate enough that it wasn't going anywhere without a moving van and many people to lift it. Mechanically it's essentially a reskin of the &quot;Enchant Talisman&quot; level five ritual, except obviously attuned to Auspex rather than a Thaumaturgy path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T04:41:25-07:00","id":1540696,"title":"","content":"Magical artifacts in any dark and immersive setting can serve as the heartbeat of any campaign. These items should never bejust tools or power-ups - they need to be woven into the very fabric of the narrative, offering players a deeper connection to the lore and the world around them. A group of characters should never stumble upon an ancient amulet or a cursed sword. It needs to be a gateway to new stories, new challenges, and new opportunities for character development.<br /> <br /> Currently i am running a game where the Lasombra Antis Sire heard about an auction of a shadow dagger on strictly enforced neutral ground. This dagger would influence obtenebration. He sent his abyss mysticism inteterested PC childer and his coterie and it was great running the auction. We had social combat with the Sabbat Lasombra (who will take revenge for the audacity soon) as well as a nice mini game that i created for this auction. The PC got the dagger and brought it to his sire, only to fall deeper and deeper into the magnetism of the abyss. In fact since they got the dagger the PC has had the &quot;opportunity&quot; to get in touch with the abyss... which led to great role play and dire consequences.<br /> <br /> In the end i use them as triggering mechanism for the plot, as reward and as motivation for players. Just be creative and do not only look at mechanical advantages. Go for narative stuff. I had the idea to for a chronicle to creat a skull that would help solve his own murder, if they would find more and more parts of the skull, which were spread over the city by demons/baali. At the start the skull would have been a bit useless, but he would always say that he needed to be &quot;whole&quot; again and with every part he would gain more and more clarity/knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T10:20:29-07:00","id":1540710,"title":"","content":"I understand the call for making artifacts &quot;special story devices&quot;, but nowadays I don't think you need to put much weight behind that. Stories will come naturally in the wake of an artifact, and there are tools to make this an easier process.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 5th edition has an interesting feature in the Dungeon Master's Guide, a set of tables, four IIRC, meant to make magical items more interesting, with things like social purpose, who created them, etc.<br /> <br /> This is a very handy feature, and an easy template to make something similar for any other game. You can then either look at it for inspiration, or roll on the table and let your imagination fill the gaps between the results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}